<Base lang="en" title="Works"><article class="prose"><p class="label">Works</p><h1>Things made can speak slowly, too.</h1><p>This is for projects, tools, and open-source work. These pages are not polished promotional copy: they will hold where a question began, what was tried, and what remains unfinished.</p><div class="grid"><section class="card"><div><span class="number">01</span><h3>Plot Ark</h3><p>An education project still moving under its own weight. It is trying to answer one question: can you spot where a student is actually stuck — a missed concept, a language barrier, or the wrong way in — before they give up on themselves? This page will fill in as the project moves, not before.</p></div><a class="arrow" href="https://schlaflied.github.io/Plot-Ark/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open Plot Ark">→</a></section><section class="card"><div><span class="number">02</span><h3>ClearCover</h3><p>A plain-language insurance policy reader. Upload a policy, get it translated clause by clause — never a purchase recommendation, only clarity. It was born on a July 2026 night spent explaining a Manulife travel-insurance policy to my parents, line by line. It later became my sandbox for practicing AEO / SEO / GEO: a deliberately everyday, easily-searched topic, the opposite of Plot Ark's ambition.</p></div><a class="arrow" href="https://github.com/Schlaflied/clearcover" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the ClearCover repository">→</a></section></div></article></Base>
